/macos/Runner/GoogleService-Info.plist

# The CocoaPods lock files. Committing them is the usual advice and it does not
# work here: nothing in this project can regenerate them except a release run.
# Both build scripts refuse a non-Darwin host, no job on a pull request builds
# iOS or macOS, and CocoaPods is a macOS-only toolchain in practice - so the
# moment a plugin bump moves a pod constraint, the committed snapshot is wrong
# and `pod install` refuses to reconcile it. That is not hypothetical: #492
# moved firebase_core 4.11.0 -> 4.15.2, whose podspec asks for
# `Firebase/CoreOnly ~> 12.19.3` while the snapshot pinned `= 12.15.0`, and
# every dev build since failed on it - a plain `pod install` keeps a locked
# version for a transitive pod even when the development pod above it changed,
# which is what CocoaPods means by "you should run `pod update`".
#
# What is lost is narrow. `pubspec.lock` still pins every plugin to an exact
# version, and each plugin's podspec pins the pods it needs, so what floats is
# only a third-party pod's patch range inside a `~>` it already declared.
# What is gained is a release that does not break on every plugin bump.
#
# The release job uploads the pair it resolved as `podfile-locks`, so this is
# reversible from real files rather than from a guess: commit that pair and
# drop these two lines.
/ios/Podfile.lock
/macos/Podfile.lock

# The native crash database, which sentry-native writes beside the executable
# unless told otherwise - so a `flutter run` from here creates it in the repo
# root. It holds an installation id and any crash not yet sent. Ignored as well
# as redirected (see Telemetry._nativeDatabasePath), because the default
# applies to any build made before that landed.
/.sentry-native/

# Local build defines, which may hold QU_CARTO_KEY and QU_BUILD_SERVER_KEY.
# See docs/releasing.md. Every name but the template, because those are real
# secrets and the filename is a free choice.
#
# test/local_defines_test.dart is the other half: an ignore rule does nothing
# against `git add -f`.
/dart-defines*.json
!/dart-defines.local.example.json

# faaccrack: the engine ships obfuscated (lib/modules/cpp/faaccrack/faaccrack.c
# is generated). Its readable source and the generator must never be committed -
# see lib/modules/cpp/faaccrack/BUILD_NOTES.md for where they live.
faaccrack.orig.c
cobf.py
verify_obf.sh
